# Application (`ForensicsAnalyzer.Application`)

- Feature folders: `{Feature}/Commands`, `{Feature}/Queries`. Commands/queries are records implementing `IRequest<T>`.
- Handlers contain use-case logic. Depend on interfaces (`IApplicationDbContext`, `I*Repository`, `ICurrentUserService`), not Infrastructure types.
- FluentValidation for writes. Permissions live in `Authorization/Permissions.cs` — new groups need an architecture question.
- No `DbContext` implementation, SQL, or Identity stores here.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — Infrastructure type in Application
public class Handler(ApplicationDbContext db) : IRequestHandler<...>

// ✅ GOOD
public class CreateCaseCommandHandler : IRequestHandler<CreateCaseCommand, Guid>
{
    public CreateCaseCommandHandler(IApplicationDbContext context, ICurrentUserService currentUser) { }
}
```

New handlers/validators require unit tests and a feature or commit doc.
